# Repository domain map and intent

## Role and context

- Explains high-level domain map, intent, history, and boundaries not inferable from structure alone.

## Repository model

- Active production, legacy reference, experimental drafts, external third-party, tests/benchmarks
- Not all folders are equal in importance

## Primary roots

- `matlab/` — production and near-production code
- `tests/` — experiments, learning, validation utilities

## Core scientific domains (mature, reusable)

- `astro/`, `image/`, `pipeline/`, `celestial/`, `timeSeries/`, `telescope/`, `VO/`
- Not ULTRASAT-specific by default

## ULTRASAT-specific domains

- `matlab/astro/+ultrasat/` and related pipeline/util/services
- Mission-specific assumptions — detailed rules in `+ultrasat/.cursor/rules/`

## Base and infrastructure

- `base/`, `util/`, `io/`, `db/`, `tools/` — cross-cutting, stay generic

## External and obsolete

- `external/` — third-party; do not modify unless intended
- `obsolete`, `Drafts-*`, `backup-*`, `old` — reference only; do not extend

## What not to do

- Do not refactor legacy/obsolete unless explicitly requested
- Do not assume all folders follow the same standards
- Do not modernize external code silently

## Output expectations

- Identify which domain you are touching
- Ask before crossing domain boundaries
